<?xml version="1.0" ?>
<usx version="3.0">
  <book code="PHP" style="id">PHILIPPIANS</book>
  <chapter number="1" style="c" sid="PHP 1"/>
  <para style="s1">Apostolic Greeting</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PHP 1:1"/>
    Paul and Timothy, bondservants wholly devoted to Christ Jesus,
    <verse eid="PHP 1:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">To all of God’s consecrated people in Christ Jesus who are living in Philippi, together with the overseers and deacons:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="PHP 1:2"/>
    May grace or undeserved favour and peace be yours from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ.
    <verse eid="PHP 1:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Pauline Thanksgiving</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="PHP 1:3"/>
    I express gratitude to my God every time I bring you to mind,
    <verse eid="PHP 1:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="PHP 1:4"/>
    constantly in every petition I make on behalf of all of you, offering my petition with delight,
    <verse eid="PHP 1:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="PHP 1:5"/>
    on account of your partnership in advancing the gospel from the very first day until this present moment,
    <verse eid="PHP 1:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="PHP 1:6"/>
    holding firmly to this conviction: that He who initiated a good work among you will bring it to completion by the day of Christ Jesus.
    <verse eid="PHP 1:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="PHP 1:7"/>
    It is entirely appropriate for me to have this perspective about all of you, because you hold a place in my heart, since all of you share with me in grace, both during my chains and in the vindication and establishment of the gospel.
    <verse eid="PHP 1:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="PHP 1:8"/>
    For God serves as my witness of how deeply I long for all of you with the tender affections that belong to Christ Jesus.
    <verse eid="PHP 1:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Pauline Prayer</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="PHP 1:9"/>
    And this is what I pray: that your love would continue to abound more and more in genuine knowledge and complete insight,
    <verse eid="PHP 1:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="PHP 1:10"/>
    enabling you to discern what is excellent, so that you would be pure and without offence for the day of Christ,
    <verse eid="PHP 1:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="PHP 1:11"/>
    having been filled with the fruit of righteousness that comes through Jesus Christ, resulting in glory and praise to God.
    <verse eid="PHP 1:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">The Furtherance of the Gospel</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="PHP 1:12"/>
    Now I want you to understand, brothers and sisters, that the circumstances surrounding me have actually resulted in the gospel’s advancement,
    <verse eid="PHP 1:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="PHP 1:13"/>
    with the result that my imprisonment for Christ has become widely known throughout the entire imperial guard and to everyone else,
    <verse eid="PHP 1:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="PHP 1:14"/>
    and the majority of the brothers and sisters, having gained confidence in the Lord through my imprisonment, now speak God’s message with greater courage and without fear.
    <verse eid="PHP 1:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="PHP 1:15"/>
    It is true that some are proclaiming Christ from motives of envy and contentiousness, while others do so from genuine goodwill.
    <verse eid="PHP 1:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="PHP 1:16"/>
    These latter ones proclaim Christ from love, understanding that I have been positioned here for the defence of the gospel.
    <verse eid="PHP 1:16"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="PHP 1:17"/>
    The former group announces Christ from selfish ambition rather than pure motives, supposing they can intensify my suffering in my chains.
    <verse eid="PHP 1:17"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="PHP 1:18"/>
    But what does it matter? The important thing is that in every manner—whether from false motives or genuine ones—Christ is being proclaimed, and I find joy in this. Indeed, I will continue to find joy,
    <verse eid="PHP 1:18"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="PHP 1:19"/>
    for I know that this situation will result in my deliverance through your intercession and the generous supply of the Spirit of Jesus Christ,
    <verse eid="PHP 1:19"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="PHP 1:20"/>
    in keeping with my eager expectation and confident hope that I will not be put to shame in any respect, but that with complete boldness—as has always been the case—Christ will be exalted in my body, whether through my life or through my death.
    <verse eid="PHP 1:20"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="PHP 1:21"/>
    For in my case, living means Christ, and dying brings gain.
    <verse eid="PHP 1:21"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="PHP 1:22"/>
    Yet if continuing to live in this physical body means productive labour for me, then I cannot say which I would prefer.
    <verse eid="PHP 1:22"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="PHP 1:23"/>
    I find myself caught between these two possibilities, having the strong desire to depart this life and be with Christ, which would be vastly superior.
    <verse eid="PHP 1:23"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="PHP 1:24"/>
    Yet remaining in this physical existence is more essential for your benefit.
    <verse eid="PHP 1:24"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="PHP 1:25"/>
    Being persuaded of this, I know that I will remain and continue alongside all of you to promote your progress and joy in the faith,
    <verse eid="PHP 1:25"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="PHP 1:26"/>
    so that your confident boasting in Christ Jesus may increase on account of me when I come to be with you again.
    <verse eid="PHP 1:26"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">The Faith of the Gospel</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="PHP 1:27"/>
    Simply ensure that you conduct yourselves in a manner that reflects the gospel of Christ, so that whether I come and observe you personally or remain absent, I may receive reports about your circumstances—that you are standing united in one spirit, striving together with one purpose for the faith that belongs to the gospel,
    <verse eid="PHP 1:27"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" sid="PHP 1:28"/>
    and not being intimidated in any way by those who oppose you. This serves as evidence of their coming destruction but of your salvation—and this comes from God.
    <verse eid="PHP 1:28"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" sid="PHP 1:29"/>
    For it has been graciously granted to you on Christ’s behalf not merely to believe in Him, but also to suffer for His sake,
    <verse eid="PHP 1:29"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" sid="PHP 1:30"/>
    as you undergo the same kind of struggle you witnessed in me and now hear that I continue to experience.
    <verse eid="PHP 1:30"/>
  </para>
  <chapter eid="PHP 1"/>
  <chapter number="2" style="c" sid="PHP 2"/>
  <para style="s1">Spiritual Unity</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PHP 2:1"/>
    Therefore, if there exists any encouragement in Christ, if any consolation flowing from love, if any fellowship created by the Spirit, if any tender compassion and mercy,
    <verse eid="PHP 2:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="PHP 2:2"/>
    complete my joy by maintaining the same mindset, possessing the same love, being united in spirit and purpose.
    <verse eid="PHP 2:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="PHP 2:3"/>
    Do nothing motivated by selfish ambition or empty conceit, but in humility regard others as more important than yourselves.
    <verse eid="PHP 2:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="PHP 2:4"/>
    Each person should be concerned not only with personal interests but also with the interests of others.
    <verse eid="PHP 2:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">The Paradigm of Christ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="PHP 2:5"/>
    Adopt the same attitude that was present in Christ Jesus,
    <verse eid="PHP 2:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="PHP 2:6"/>
    who, though He existed in the very form of God, did not regard His equality with God as something to exploit for His own advantage,
    <verse eid="PHP 2:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="PHP 2:7"/>
    but instead emptied Himself by assuming the form of a slave, being born in human likeness.
    <verse eid="PHP 2:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="PHP 2:8"/>
    And having been recognised in His manner as a man, He humbled Himself by becoming obedient to the point of death—even death on a cross.
    <verse eid="PHP 2:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="PHP 2:9"/>
    For this reason God also highly exalted Him and bestowed on Him the name that stands above every name,
    <verse eid="PHP 2:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="PHP 2:10"/>
    so that at the name of Jesus every knee should bend—in heaven and on earth and beneath the earth—
    <verse eid="PHP 2:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="PHP 2:11"/>
    and every tongue should openly declare that Jesus Christ is Lord, to the glory of God the Father.
    <verse eid="PHP 2:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Working out of Salvation</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="PHP 2:12"/>
    Therefore, my dear ones, just as you have consistently obeyed, not only during my presence but even more so now during my absence, continue working out your salvation with reverence and trembling.
    <verse eid="PHP 2:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="PHP 2:13"/>
    For it is God who is actively at work within you, producing both the desire and the ability to accomplish His good purpose.
    <verse eid="PHP 2:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="PHP 2:14"/>
    Carry out everything without complaining and disputing,
    <verse eid="PHP 2:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="PHP 2:15"/>
    so that you may prove yourselves to be blameless and innocent, children of God who are above reproach in the midst of a warped and corrupt generation, among whom you appear as luminaries in the world,
    <verse eid="PHP 2:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="PHP 2:16"/>
    holding fast to the message of life, giving me reason for boasting on the day of Christ that I did not run my race pointlessly nor labour without result.
    <verse eid="PHP 2:16"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="PHP 2:17"/>
    But even if my life is being poured out like a drink offering upon the sacrifice and priestly service of your faith, I am filled with joy, and I share that joy with all of you.
    <verse eid="PHP 2:17"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="PHP 2:18"/>
    In the same manner, you also should be filled with joy and share that joy with me.
    <verse eid="PHP 2:18"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Timothy and Epaphroditus</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="PHP 2:19"/>
    I am confident in the Lord Jesus that I will be able to send Timothy to you soon, so that I too may be encouraged when I receive information about your circumstances.
    <verse eid="PHP 2:19"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="PHP 2:20"/>
    For I have no one else with a disposition like his who will genuinely be concerned about your welfare.
    <verse eid="PHP 2:20"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="PHP 2:21"/>
    For they all pursue their own interests rather than the interests of Jesus Christ.
    <verse eid="PHP 2:21"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="PHP 2:22"/>
    But you know Timothy’s tested character—how like a son serving alongside his father, he has laboured with me in advancing the gospel.
    <verse eid="PHP 2:22"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="PHP 2:23"/>
    I am hoping, therefore, to send him as soon as I gain clarity about my own situation,
    <verse eid="PHP 2:23"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="PHP 2:24"/>
    though I am confident in the Lord that I myself will also come to you before long.
    <verse eid="PHP 2:24"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="PHP 2:25"/>
    However, I have concluded it necessary to send Epaphroditus back to you—my brother, fellow worker, and fellow soldier, whom you sent as your representative and servant to address my needs,
    <verse eid="PHP 2:25"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="PHP 2:26"/>
    since he has been deeply longing to see all of you and was distressed that you heard about his illness.
    <verse eid="PHP 2:26"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="PHP 2:27"/>
    For indeed he was ill to the point of nearly dying, but God showed mercy to him—and not only to him but also to me—so that I would not experience one sorrow on top of another.
    <verse eid="PHP 2:27"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" sid="PHP 2:28"/>
    I am sending him back with special urgency, therefore, so that when you see him again you may experience joy, and I may have less anxiety.
    <verse eid="PHP 2:28"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" sid="PHP 2:29"/>
    Welcome him in the Lord with complete joy, and hold people like him in high honour,
    <verse eid="PHP 2:29"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" sid="PHP 2:30"/>
    because for the sake of Christ’s work he came close to death, risking his life to provide the service to me that you were unable to give personally.
    <verse eid="PHP 2:30"/>
  </para>
  <chapter eid="PHP 2"/>
  <chapter number="3" style="c" sid="PHP 3"/>
  <para style="s1">Confidence in the Righteousness Through Faith in Christ Jesus</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PHP 3:1"/>
    Finally, my brothers and sisters, find your joy in the Lord. Writing these same things to you is no burden for me, and it provides protection for you.
    <verse eid="PHP 3:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="PHP 3:2"/>
    Be on guard against the dogs! Be on guard against those who do evil! Be on guard against those who mutilate the flesh!
    <verse eid="PHP 3:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="PHP 3:3"/>
    For we are the true circumcision—we who worship by the Spirit of God and boast in Christ Jesus and place no confidence in human credentials,
    <verse eid="PHP 3:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="PHP 3:4"/>
    though I myself have grounds for confidence even in human credentials. If anyone else presumes to have confidence based on human credentials, I possess even more:
    <verse eid="PHP 3:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="PHP 3:5"/>
    circumcised on the eighth day, belonging to the people of Israel, from the tribe of Benjamin, a Hebrew descended from Hebrews; regarding the Law, a Pharisee;
    <verse eid="PHP 3:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="PHP 3:6"/>
    regarding zeal, one who persecuted the church; regarding the righteousness found in the Law, blameless.
    <verse eid="PHP 3:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="PHP 3:7"/>
    But whatever things were assets to me, I have come to regard as loss for the sake of Christ.
    <verse eid="PHP 3:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="PHP 3:8"/>
    More than that, I regard everything as loss compared to the surpassing value of knowing Christ Jesus my Lord, for whose sake I have forfeited everything and consider it all as rubbish, in order that I may gain Christ
    <verse eid="PHP 3:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="PHP 3:9"/>
    and be found in Him, not possessing my own righteousness derived from the Law, but the righteousness that comes through faith in Christ—the righteousness from God based on faith—
    <verse eid="PHP 3:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="PHP 3:10"/>
    so that I may know Him and the power of His resurrection and the sharing of His sufferings, being conformed to His death,
    <verse eid="PHP 3:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="PHP 3:11"/>
    hoping that somehow I may attain the resurrection from the dead.
    <verse eid="PHP 3:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Pressing Forward Towards the Goal</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="PHP 3:12"/>
    Not that I have already obtained this or have already reached perfection, but I press forward to take hold of it because I was also taken hold of by Christ Jesus.
    <verse eid="PHP 3:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="PHP 3:13"/>
    Brothers and sisters, I do not consider that I have already taken hold of it. But this one thing I do: forgetting what lies behind and straining towards what lies ahead,
    <verse eid="PHP 3:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="PHP 3:14"/>
    I press on towards the goal to win the prize of God’s heavenly calling in Christ Jesus.
    <verse eid="PHP 3:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="PHP 3:15"/>
    Therefore, let all of us who are mature adopt this way of thinking. And if on any point you think differently, God will clarify this for you as well.
    <verse eid="PHP 3:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="PHP 3:16"/>
    Nevertheless, let us live according to the same standard we have already reached.
    <verse eid="PHP 3:16"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">The Apostolic Pattern</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="PHP 3:17"/>
    Brothers and sisters, join together in imitating me, and pay careful attention to those who conduct themselves according to the pattern we have provided for you.
    <verse eid="PHP 3:17"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="PHP 3:18"/>
    For many people conduct themselves—about whom I have frequently warned you, and now tell you even with tears—as enemies of the cross of Christ.
    <verse eid="PHP 3:18"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="PHP 3:19"/>
    Their end is destruction, their god is their appetite, and they take pride in their shame—they set their minds on earthly matters.
    <verse eid="PHP 3:19"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="PHP 3:20"/>
    But our citizenship belongs to heaven, and it is from there we eagerly await a Saviour, the Lord Jesus Christ,
    <verse eid="PHP 3:20"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="PHP 3:21"/>
    who will transform our lowly bodies to be conformed to His glorious body, according to the power by which He is able to subject all things to Himself.
    <verse eid="PHP 3:21"/>
  </para>
  <chapter eid="PHP 3"/>
  <chapter number="4" style="c" sid="PHP 4"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PHP 4:1"/>
    Therefore, my brothers and sisters whom I love and long for deeply, my joy and crown, continue standing firm in the Lord in this manner, dear ones.
    <verse eid="PHP 4:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Exhortation to Unity</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="PHP 4:2"/>
    I urge Euodia and I urge Syntyche to achieve harmony of mind in the Lord.
    <verse eid="PHP 4:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="PHP 4:3"/>
    Yes, I also ask you, my true companion, to assist these women who laboured alongside me in spreading the gospel, together with Clement and my other fellow workers, whose names are recorded in the book of life.
    <verse eid="PHP 4:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Final Exhortations</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="PHP 4:4"/>
    Find joy in the Lord always; again I say, find joy.
    <verse eid="PHP 4:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="PHP 4:5"/>
    Let your gracious spirit be evident to all people. The Lord is near.
    <verse eid="PHP 4:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="PHP 4:6"/>
    Do not be anxious about anything, but in every situation, through prayer and petition accompanied by thanksgiving, present your requests to God.
    <verse eid="PHP 4:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="PHP 4:7"/>
    And the peace of God, which surpasses all human understanding, will guard your hearts and your thoughts in Christ Jesus.
    <verse eid="PHP 4:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="PHP 4:8"/>
    Finally, brothers and sisters, whatever is true, whatever is honourable, whatever is right, whatever is pure, whatever is lovely, whatever is admirable—if anything possesses excellence, and if anything deserves praise—focus your thoughts on these things.
    <verse eid="PHP 4:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="PHP 4:9"/>
    Whatever you have learned and received and heard and observed in me—put these things into practice. And the God of peace will be with you.
    <verse eid="PHP 4:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Contentment in Every Situation</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="PHP 4:10"/>
    I experienced great joy in the Lord that now at last you have renewed your concern for me, though you were indeed concerned but lacked opportunity to demonstrate it.
    <verse eid="PHP 4:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="PHP 4:11"/>
    I am not saying this because I am in need, for I have learned to be content in whatever circumstances I find myself.
    <verse eid="PHP 4:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="PHP 4:12"/>
    I know what it is to experience deprivation, and I know what it is to live in abundance. In every circumstance and in all situations, I have learned the secret of both being well-fed and going hungry, both having plenty and experiencing scarcity.
    <verse eid="PHP 4:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="PHP 4:13"/>
    I have strength for all things through Him who empowers me.
    <verse eid="PHP 4:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="PHP 4:14"/>
    Nevertheless, you acted nobly in sharing together with me in my hardship.
    <verse eid="PHP 4:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="PHP 4:15"/>
    You Philippians yourselves also know that in the early period of the gospel ministry, when I left Macedonia, no church entered into partnership with me regarding financial support except you alone;
    <verse eid="PHP 4:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="PHP 4:16"/>
    for even when I was in Thessalonica, you sent assistance for my needs on multiple occasions.
    <verse eid="PHP 4:16"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="PHP 4:17"/>
    Not that I am seeking the gift itself, but I am seeking the benefit that accumulates to your account.
    <verse eid="PHP 4:17"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="PHP 4:18"/>
    I have received everything in full and have more than enough. I am amply supplied, having received from Epaphroditus the gifts you sent—a fragrant offering, an acceptable sacrifice that pleases God.
    <verse eid="PHP 4:18"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="PHP 4:19"/>
    And my God will fully supply every need of yours according to His glorious riches in Christ Jesus.
    <verse eid="PHP 4:19"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="PHP 4:20"/>
    Now to our God and Father be glory forever and ever. Amen.
    <verse eid="PHP 4:20"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Final Greetings and Benediction</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="PHP 4:21"/>
    Greet every one of God’s people in Christ Jesus. The brothers and sisters who are with me send you greetings.
    <verse eid="PHP 4:21"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="PHP 4:22"/>
    All of God’s people here send you greetings, especially those who belong to Caesar’s household.
    <verse eid="PHP 4:22"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="PHP 4:23"/>
    May the grace of the Lord Jesus Christ be with your spirit. Amen.
    <verse eid="PHP 4:23"/>
  </para>
  <chapter eid="PHP 4"/>
</usx>
